I now have a solid understanding of the game loop flow:

- WIN_MainLoop: Hangar → ShipComp → Load map (RAP_LoadMap) → Do_Game → If energy <= 0, death → Otherwise advance to next wave (game_wave++), INTRO_Landing between waves. When game_wave == dwrap (diff_wrap[difficulty]-1), the sector is complete.

In the case of DIFF_2 (normal), diff_wrap is probably = {3, 9, 9, 9}? Let me check diff_wrap. In shareware: game 1 has 9 waves (MAP1G1..MAP9G1). Let me search for diff_wrap.

Also RAP_DisplayShieldLevel — I need to read that.

Next, the sound format. Let me look at audiolib. The Apogee Sound System format (Apogee Sound System - "SND" format): 52-byte header:
```
WORD size;        // Total file size
WORD version;     // 0x0111
WORD type;        // 1 = 8-bit, 2 = 8-bit signed, 3 = 8-bit unsigned, 4 = 8-bit signed
WORD reserved;
WORD volume;
WORD loop;
WORD loopstart;
WORD loopend;
DWORD rate;
...
```
The actual Apogee sound header (from the DMX / Apogee Sound System documentation):

```
struct {
  WORD size;
  WORD version;
  WORD type;
  WORD reserved;
  WORD volume;
  WORD loop;
  WORD loop_start;
  WORD loop_end;
  DWORD rate;
  CHAR name[8];
  WORD size_of_header;   // = 0x12 (18) in the old format?
  WORD size_of_data;
}
```

To get the exact format, let me check the audiolib source. Let me take a look at the audiolib directory.

